## What it was

DMZ (dmz.fun, first designed under the working name meme.tech) was a mobile-first Solana app for memecoin trading. It combined trading, token discovery and a social layer in one place. You could buy, sell and swap any memecoin in a few taps, pay with a bank account or Apple Pay, and launch your own token for free, all through a smart wallet so no crypto knowledge was needed.

The pitch was "trade together, win together": a social feed of tokens and trends, voice chat rooms, following friends and top traders, plus quests and leaderboards. Behind that sat a DEX that pooled liquidity from the major Solana platforms.

## My role

I designed the brand and the product: the identity, the mobile app's trading, discovery, social and token-launch flows, and the design language behind them. The hard part was making a fast, risky, jargon-heavy market feel friendly and simple without hiding what was going on.

